# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QLNN_iter (trained as QLNN_iter_8 / sat3tglf_v8) — TGLF settings of the
# training database (ITER,
# production_run_4 / sat3_em_azf-1 flux-matching corpus, "sat3_em_iter4",
# Aug 2026).
#
# The switches in the "database settings" block were forced onto every case
# by the database generator on top of the FUSE
# flux-matching input.tglf: SAT_RULE=3 in CGYRO units, electromagnetic
# (USE_BPER/USE_BPAR), ALPHA_ZF=-1, NBASIS_MAX=6, KYGRID_MODEL=4 / NKY=12,
# NMODES=2, USE_MHD_RULE=false, USE_AVE_ION_GRID=true (note: TRUE for this
# corpus, unlike the DIII-D QLNN_d3d_1 database). A QLNN prediction is only
# meaningful with these settings: the QL weights were computed with them, and
# run_qlnn feeds them through TJLF's saturation rule with the SAT_RULE /
# ALPHA_ZF / UNITS of the input it is given, so pass them as here.
#
# Species layout: the DATABASE ran TGLF with NS=4 unbundled species
# (1 = e, 2 = D, 3 = T, 4 = one lumped impurity as FUSE builds it from the
# ITER mix; the FUSE input.tglf also lists a 5th, heavy species which NS=4
# excludes). The NEURAL NETS were trained on the (e, DT, imp) lumping of
# those inputs (35 inputs). run_qlnn lumps an NS=4/5 input automatically via
# `qlnn_lump_dt` (AS_2+AS_3; TAUS/RLTS/RLNS/VPAR density-weighted; MASS_2 =
# density-weighted D/T mass in m_D units, 1.00 pure D .. 1.25 for 50/50 D-T —
# MASS_2 varies over the flux-matching history and is a live feature;
# impurity slot 4 -> 3). An NS=3 (e, DT, imp) input — what FUSE produces with
# act.ActorTGLF.lump_ions = true — is used as is.
#
# VEXB_SHEAR: the inputs of this corpus predate the mid-2026 runTGLFdb sign
# fix (vexb_convention = legacy): VEXB_SHEAR is opposite in sign to
# VPAR_SHEAR_1 here (TGYRO convention would be same-sign). TurbulentTransport
# applies the SIGN_BT flip for legacy bundles itself. VEXB_SHEAR operating
# points were excluded from training (post-linear quench only) but
# VEXB_SHEAR remains an input feature.
#
# Physics values below are a real case from the database (tglfdb entry
# input.tglf_000001 at rho = 0.25, flux-matching iteration history of an ITER
# FUSE case; r/R = 0.086). Replace them with your own; keep the switches.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

